; Comparing an account total with a number, or an account total in one
; commodity with an amount, answers on every run.
;
; A number has no commodity, so `total < 100` compares every component of
; Assets:Mixed, which holds $5.00 and 10 EUR, with it, and holds.  An
; account in one commodity compares as its amount does: Liabilities:Card's
; $-5.00 is below $3.00 and Expenses:Food's $5.00 is above it.
;
; Comparing Assets:Mixed with an amount in dollars is an error, which
; value-compare-mixed-balance-error.test pins on this same journal; the
; error blocks live there so that the semantic bisimulation, which skips
; a file with any, still replays this journal.

2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Mixed    $5.00
    Assets:Mixed    10 EUR
    Equity

2024/01/02 Lunch
    Expenses:Food       $5.00
    Liabilities:Card

test bal Assets -d 'total < 100'
               $5.00
              10 EUR  Assets:Mixed
end test

test bal Expenses Liabilities -d 'total < $3'
              $-5.00  Liabilities:Card
end test

test bal Expenses Liabilities -d 'total > $3'
               $5.00  Expenses:Food
end test
